---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Asavin Wattanajantra, an Editorial Intelligence practitioner working across research, narrative, content strategy and organisational knowledge systems."
  pageType="profile"
>
  <div class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">About</p>
        <h1 class="t-heading mb-6">{SITE.author}</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          {SITE.title}
        </p>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <div class="about-photo mb-16">
        <img src="/Images/asavin.jpg" alt="Asavin Wattanajantra" class="about-img" />
      </div>

      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          I'm an Editorial Intelligence practitioner — working at the intersection of qualitative research, editorial judgement, narrative and knowledge systems to help organisations understand what they know, discover what they need to learn and build positions that compound over time.
        </p>
        <p>
          The ideas on this site emerged from practical work — most extensively at Sage, where programmes like <a href="/narratives/hidden-hours" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">Hidden Hours</a>, <a href="/narratives/winning-in-small" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">Winning in Small</a> and <a href="/narratives/trusted-ai" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">Trusted AI</a> developed into something beyond content campaigns: knowledge systems designed to strengthen with every new cycle of evidence.
        </p>

        <h2>Where this came from</h2>
        <p>
          Editorial Intelligence grew from two decades of practice across journalism, publishing, content strategy, thought leadership and research programmes. One instinct connected the work: the most valuable thing to do with evidence isn't simply publish it, but connect it, develop it and let it inform what comes next.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI made accumulated knowledge faster to structure and navigate. It did not decide what the evidence meant. That gap — between evidence collected and evidence understood — gave a name to the discipline I'd been practising.
        </p>
        <p style="font-style: italic; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); padding-left: 1.25rem;">
          Editorial Intelligence.
        </p>

        <h2>How the practice developed</h2>
        <p>
          I began as a technology journalist at publications including <a href="https://www.itpro.com/author/asavin-wattanajantra/page/2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">IT Pro</a> and <a href="https://www.cnet.com/profiles/asavin-wattanajantra/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">CNET</a>, learning to question claims, interpret technical subjects and find what matters to an audience.
        </p>
        <p>
          At <a href="https://www.redconsultancy.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">RED Consultancy</a>, I applied that judgement in PR and communications, developing thought leadership, reports and campaign narratives for technology and corporate clients.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Metia, I translated complex products and ideas for developer and IT audiences, including through an <a href="https://metia.com/blog/always-on-content-and-paid-social-media-marketing-with-microsoft/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">always-on Microsoft developer-community programme</a> connecting editorial judgement, audience evidence and distribution.
        </p>
        <p>
          As marketing manager at open-source agency Deeson, I worked where technical expertise, community and commercial positioning meet.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Sage, the practice expanded into research-led narratives including Hidden Hours, Winning in Small and Trusted AI. Editorial Intelligence is the synthesis: editorial judgement applied to evidence, expertise and organisational knowledge.
        </p>

        <h2>The discipline, the OS, the consulting</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Editorial Intelligence</strong> is the discipline: how organisations develop evidence into better decisions, stronger narratives and reusable knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong><a href="/editorial-intelligence-os" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">Editorial Intelligence OS</a></strong> makes it repeatable through frameworks, methods, assessments and AI workflows.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong><a href="/work" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">Consulting</a></strong> applies it to an organisation's editorial capability, narrative systems and evidence infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>Writing portfolio</h2>
        <p>
          My published work — articles, research narratives and editorial projects — is collected on Authory.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://authory.com/asavin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">
            authory.com/asavin
          </a>
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          If you're working on similar problems — connecting organisational knowledge, building editorial systems, or thinking about AI and strategic content — I'd like to hear from you.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm also speaking with practitioners outside my own B2B technology context to pressure-test Editorial Intelligence. <a href="/compare-notes" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] no-underline hover:underline">See the open invitation to compare notes →</a>
        </p>

        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co" class="contact-link">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="1" y="3" width="14" height="10" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25"/>
              <path d="M1 5l7 5 7-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            asavin@editorialintelligence.co
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashwat/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="1" y="1" width="14" height="14" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25"/>
              <path d="M4 6.5v5M4 4v.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <path d="M7.5 11.5V9a2 2 0 014 0v2.5M7.5 6.5v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            linkedin.com/in/ashwat
          </a>
          <a href="https://authory.com/asavin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M3 4h10M3 8h7M3 12h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            authory.com/asavin
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="divider mt-16 mb-10" />

      <a href="/start" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.375rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--color-accent);text-decoration:none;">
        New to Editorial Intelligence? Start here →
      </a>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-prose p,
  .about-prose h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-prose p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .about-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .contact-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.625rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.15s;
  }

  .contact-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .contact-link svg {
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .about-photo {
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 480px;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 6px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
</style>
